From 8255e0f70104a09945917f22ca0d548854fc9ca1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:18:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10215/11362] exp6527: pin the V565 input state; the Exp6526
 mirror follows its source

Team-lead routing items 2 and 3 from the verdict_class batch.

test_experiment_6527 was pre-existing broken (6 failures at e187fc8a31,
before this batch): its fixture rebuilt from the LIVE tree, so it broke
when the roadmap rotated past V565 and again when exp6520's
flagged_adversarial stamp was cleared on 2026-08-29 as a false
positive. The fixture now mirrors the exact input state the run read -
commit ab2a4b946a (V565 activation), verified 7/7 against the hashes in
exp6527's own immutable_input_receipts - while the live Exp6520
rechecks stay live, which is the corrigendum's own design (historical
reads plus current-code recheck). Same stale-live-state repair class as
3fddef1bf0's test_6526/test_6687 fixtures.

The writer's recompute_exp6526 baked "verdict_class_from_rows":
"partial" - a frozen mirror of the declaration Exp6526 corrected to
null in a33755953d. Rather than swap one constant for another, the
mirror now reads the value from the source artifact, so it is right
against both the pinned historical input and the corrected live one.
A synthetic-payload test pins the derivation (the pinned fixture alone
could not: its V565-era input also says partial); mutation back to the
constant goes RED, restore byte-identical.

Suite: 8 passed (was 3 failed against live state, 6 at pre-change).

